# sudogate — lets __USER__ run ONLY the wrapper as root, without a password.
#
# The wrapper takes no command on its command line: it takes a token naming a
# record the gate daemon wrote after the owner approved the command on their
# phone. That record lives in /run/sudogate/approved, mode 0700 under the
# daemon's own account, so __USER__ can neither read a token nor write a
# record. The wrapper re-classifies the command with the root-owned patterns
# in /etc/sudogate/destructive.patterns and, when destructive, requires a
# valid TOTP — carried in the record and checked against /etc/sudogate/seed
# (0400 root), which neither __USER__ nor the daemon can read.
#
# Install at 0440 root:root. Files with wider permissions are ignored silently.
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/sudogate-run
